The client needed to combine the best aspects of two different leasing services into one cohesive offering. The goal was to make it distinct enough from the rest of the site that users could easily navigate, find the information they were looking for, and order a car that fit their needs for a monthly fee.

Content strategy and UI wireframes went hand in hand. Together with the team, we explored the best ways to make useful content clearly accessible to users. We put forward a few proposals and, through discussion, arrived at the model that went into final production.

The project was delivered on a fast schedule, and after the first release we were able to keep refining the UI and content using real performance metrics.

We had fairly free rein to ideate, and the result of that creative work is here. The interface supports the content, and the functionality was designed to be as simple and user-centered as possible. Everything unnecessary has been stripped away, leaving just the path to worry-free driving.
